From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 03:22:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] sf_smac: update the connected AP's BSS entry from its beacons

get_station reads a client's DTIM period from the TIM element of the
AP's beacon in cfg80211's BSS entry. The entry is only ever written from
scan results, which hold whatever frame the firmware heard. An AP found
by an active scan, as a 5 GHz AP usually is, has only probe response
IEs, which carry no TIM, so the client showed "dtim period: 0".

The driver passes every beacon it receives to cfg80211 as an OBSS beacon
only. Also inform cfg80211 of the connected AP's beacons, as mac80211
does, so its entry has beacon IEs whatever band and scan found it.

Signed-off-by: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
---
 sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/fullmac/siwifi_rx.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/fullmac/siwifi_rx.c b/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/fullmac/siwifi_rx.c
index df918e4..f940f54 100644
--- a/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/fullmac/siwifi_rx.c
+++ b/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/fullmac/siwifi_rx.c
@@ -653,6 +653,26 @@ static void siwifi_rx_mgmt(struct siwifi_hw *siwifi_hw, struct siwifi_vif *siwif
                                         hw_rxhdr->phy_info.phy_prim20_freq,
                                         rxvect->rssi1);
         }
+        /*
+         * The connected AP's beacon also updates its BSS entry, as mac80211
+         * does, so the entry has beacon IEs (the DTIM period in its TIM)
+         * when the scan that found the AP saw only a probe response.
+         */
+        if (SIWIFI_VIF_TYPE(siwifi_vif) == NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION &&
+            siwifi_vif->sta.ap &&
+            ether_addr_equal(mgmt->bssid, siwifi_vif->sta.ap->mac_addr)) {
+            struct ieee80211_channel *chan;
+            struct cfg80211_bss *bss = NULL;
+
+            chan = ieee80211_get_channel(siwifi_hw->wiphy,
+                                         hw_rxhdr->phy_info.phy_prim20_freq);
+            if (chan)
+                bss = cfg80211_inform_bss_frame(siwifi_hw->wiphy, chan, mgmt,
+                                                skb->len, rxvect->rssi1 * 100,
+                                                GFP_ATOMIC);
+            if (bss)
+                cfg80211_put_bss(siwifi_hw->wiphy, bss);
+        }
         siwifi_vif->mgmt_stats.rx_bcn_cnts++;
     } else if ((ieee80211_is_deauth(mgmt->frame_control) ||
                 ieee80211_is_disassoc(mgmt->frame_control)) &&
